From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: mirror QSEED fetch under final reflection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The final DPU pipe orientation can add horizontal and vertical reflection
when DRM rotation is converted into the rotator's clockwise representation.
QSEED derives directional fetch extensions from the unreflected source and
extended rectangles, so the left/right and top/bottom fields must follow the
final reflected orientation.

On TB322FC with left 90-degree rotation, the primary pipe retains source
y=0 while programming both reflection bits. It programs top=0 and bottom=6,
but the final reflection requires the directional fetch to be interpreted
from the opposite side of the physical extent. The previous programming
correlates with UBWC error 0x00ff0001 and a half-panel failure. Mirroring
fetch directions under final reflection preserves the same physical extent
and fetch totals.

This changes only the directional PE fetch fields. QSEED phase, preload and
source totals, source rectangles, UBWC and source-split ordering are
unchanged. The no-reflection right 270-degree path retains its existing
programming.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
@@ -600,6 +600,10 @@ static void dpu_plane_setup_qseed3_v11(struct dpu_sw_pipe_cfg *pipe_cfg,
 	fetch_right = ext->x2 - src->x2;
 	fetch_top = src->y1 - ext->y1;
 	fetch_btm = ext->y2 - src->y2;
+	if (pipe_cfg->rotation & DRM_MODE_REFLECT_X)
+		swap(fetch_left, fetch_right);
+	if (pipe_cfg->rotation & DRM_MODE_REFLECT_Y)
+		swap(fetch_top, fetch_btm);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < DPU_MAX_PLANES; i++) {
 		pixel_ext->left_ftch[i] = fetch_left;
